 C/6A:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/6A - write the M10 characters packed in ACC to the file at
C M12.  C/7A takes its packed characters by address, so keep the
C word in the runtime scratch location M1+5 and point M11 there.
C
C   ACC = packed characters
C   M10 = character count (at most six)
C   M12 = the FILE record
C   M13 = return link
C
C C/7A consumes exactly M10 characters; embedded NULs do not end
C this counted form.
C===========================================================
 C/7A:          ,SUBP,
                1,ATX,5        . Save the packed word in runtime scratch
                1,UTC,5        . C := address of that scratch word
               11,VTM,         . M11 := packed-character address
                 ,UJ,C/7A      . Tail-call the counted array writer
                 ,END,
